iled into the application or derived from constants. Where the bytes come from decides it.', 'expected': 'a randomized byte[]', 'source_location': 'MarketPriceFetcher.java:126', 'runtime_observation': 'Reported in 3 run(s) of the app; each run starts from a clean, read-only emulator. Fingerprint of the byte[] material (vfp; the value itself is not logged): 1 distinct value(s) over 3 reporting run(s). One value across runs means constant material on this one emulated device; varying values mean bytes generated or read at run time. Mechanical constant check of this site (IVPARAMETERSPEC-NOBS-00): verdict=constant; evidence: runs=3; distinct_vfp=1; vfp=sha256:1646421f930a38c9'}, 'repository_guidance': [{'path': 'README.md', 'content': "## How To Build\n\n[![AEFeinstein](https://github.com/AEFeinstein/mtg-familiar/actions/workflows/android.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/AEFeinstein/mtg-familiar/actions)\n\n- Download and install the latest [Android Studio](https://developer.android.com/sdk/index.html)\n- Make sure you have installed the latest Android SDK Platform, Android SDK Tools, Android SDK Platform-tools, Android SDK Build-tools, Android Support Repository, Android Support Library, and Google Play Services from the Android SDK manager\n- Check out this project with Android Studio's VCS tools\n- Press the build button\n\n## Become an Official Beta Tester\nTo receive official beta builds through Google Play, opt-in to the [beta program here](https://play.google.com/apps/testing/com.gelakinetic.mtgfam)."}], 'branch_policy': {}, 'compatibility_policy': {}, 'migration_assessment': {'usage_kind': 'unknown', 'evidence': ['fetch constructs an IvParameterSpec using sk.getEncoded() as its sole constructor argument.', 'The source-level IV argument is derived from R.string.key_lastLegalityUpdate, a value compiled into the application, through SecretKeySpec and SecretKey.getEncoded().', 'The CrySL specification requires randomized[iv] for either governed IvParameterSpec constructor event and ensures preparedIV[this] after the event.', 'When the decrypt helper is invoked from this path, it obtains AES/CBC/PKCS5Padding and initializes it in DECRYPT_MODE with the constructed IV parameter and the same SecretKey.', 'In the three reported runtime executions, the byte material reaching the governed call had one distinct fingerprint.', 'The supplied evidence does not establish a security impact beyond the violated static randomized-provenance requirement.'], 'legacy_compatibility_required': True, 'safe_strategy': 'Replace the key-derived IV protocol rather than generating a new IV during decryption. The encryption-side producer must generate an unpredictable CBC IV per encryption, store or transmit that IV with the ciphertext in a versioned/self-describing representation, and the decryption path must recover that record-specific IV. Existing ciphertext must be re-encrypted, migrated, or explicitly retired before removal of the fixed-IV path; a decryption fallback that reconstructs the same key-derived IV would retain the reported predicate.', 'policy_authorized': False}, 'publication_considerations': [{'category': 'compatibility_contract', 'description': 'Publication requires confirmation that encryption producers emit a record-specific IV and that stored, cached, or externally delivered legacy ciphertext remains supported through an approved migration or is intentionally retired. Gradle builds, unit tests, Android-test compilation, and source-level predicate rechecks cannot establish that external or persisted-value contract.', 'kind': 'Ciphertext producer and compatibility review', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['CLM-002', 'CLM-004', 'CLM-006']}], 'digest_contract_assessment': {'security_relevance': 'false', 'contract_kind': 'unknown', 'expected_digest_source': '', 'backend_repository_available': False, 'backend_change_required': False, 'client_only_change_safe': False, 'rollout_strategy': '', 'pull_request_note': ''}, 'review_assumptions': ['MarketPriceFetcher obtains its encrypted payload through a different binding or direct connection not evidenced in the supplied TcgpApi source.', 'The producer contract must specify the response declaration name, JSON field names/types for version, ciphertext, and IV metadata, and the TcgpApi method or endpoint to which it applies before this file can be changed safely.', 'Persisted and external protocol compatibility is unresolved; no legacy envelope fallback can be added from the available evidence.', 'The existing embedded ciphertext and resource-derived AES key are required for the currently shipped token-acquisition flow; removing them without a producer-issued replacement would break that flow.', 'The required approved ciphertext-record schema, its TcgpApi response declaration, endpoint, and compatibility policy have not been supplied. Consequently, MarketPriceFetcher cannot recover a record-specific IV without inventing a cross-file API.', 'The producer contract must establish the encoding of IV metadata and whether absent, malformed, or legacy records must be supported before fetch can migrate from the shipped credentials.', 'MarketPriceFetcher.decrypt(String, String, SecretKey, IvParameterSpec) remains the testable validation/decryption operation used by fetch, as provided by the sibling API surface and previous file contract.', "The current Android Base64 implementation is compatible with MarketPriceFetcher.decrypt's ciphertext-string representation; the test generates ciphertext only in memory and does not assert or introduce a persisted or protocol format.", 'The missing producer-approved versioned ciphertext-envelope schema prevents this test from directly constructing an envelope object. Once that schema and its consuming API are approved, this test may need to be migrated to exercise that API directly.', 'Malformed IV rejection is asserted as any exception because the supplied contracts require rejection but do not specify whether validation reports IllegalArgumentException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, or another exception type.'], 'review_blockers': [], 'required_tests': ['After the producer contract identifies the applicable API binding, add the planned envelope validation/decryption tests against the MarketPriceFetcher seam using the approved response type.', 'Create the planned MarketPriceFetcherCiphertextEnvelopeTest only after the approved envelope-binding API exists; it must verify matching record IV decryption and rejection of missing, malformed, and wrong-length IV metadata before decryption.', 'Add a regression test for MarketPriceFetcher.decrypt rejecting a null or incorrect-length IvParameterSpec before Cipher.init when a compilable test source and supported test classpath are supplied.', 'Run MarketPriceFetcherCiphertextEnvelopeTest on the Android test classpath to verify matching-IV decryption and rejection of absent, empty, and non-block-length IV inputs.'], 'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'manual_review_required': True, 'auto_apply': False, 'publication_allowed': False, 'publication_status': 'blocked', 'semantic_validation': {'status': 'valid', 'errors': [], 'warnings': []}, 'stored_value_contract': {}, 'fix_scope': 'validation_only', 'status': 'SUCCESS', 'error': None, 'original_method_body': '    public static String decrypt(String algorithm, String cipherText, SecretKey key,\n                                 IvParameterSpec iv) throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException,\n            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException {\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(algorithm);\n        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, iv);\n        byte[] plainText = cipher.doFinal(Base64.getDecoder().decode(cipherText));\n        return new String(plainText);\n    }', 'corrected_method_body': '    public static String decrypt(String algorithm, String cipherText, SecretKey key,\n                                 IvParameterSpec iv) throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException,\n            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException {\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(algorithm);\n        if (iv == null || iv.getIV() == null || iv.getIV().length != cipher.getBlockSize()) {\n            throw new InvalidAlgorithmParameterException("IV must match the cipher block length");\n        }\n        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, iv);\n        byte[] plainText = cipher.doFinal(Base64.getDecoder().decode(cipherText));\n        return new String(plainText);\n    }', 'finding_id': 'e8f0a6ad109e', 'branch': 'fix/fetch-ivparameterspecspec-e8f0a6ad109e-8fac4604a3', 'base_branch': 'master', 'base_commit': '18477bcf55df765bf8be67e56fb468529249fe8e', 'solution_revision': '8fac4604a3', 'worktree_attempt': 1, 'orphaned_worktree_paths': [], 'worktree_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final/finding_worktrees/com.gelakinetic.mtgfam_99.apk/e8f0a6ad109e/8fac4604a3', 'base_repository_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final/clones/com.gelakinetic.mtgfam_99.apk', 'coordinated_edits': [{'source_file': 'mobile/src/main/java/com/gelakinetic/mtgfam/helpers/tcgp/MarketPriceFetcher.java', 'symbol': 'MarketPriceFetcher.decrypt', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '    public static String decrypt(String algorithm, String cipherText, SecretKey key,\n                                 IvParameterSpec iv) throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException,\n            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException {\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(algorithm);\n        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, iv);\n        byte[] plainText = cipher.doFinal(Base64.getDecoder().decode(cipherText));\n        return new String(plainText);\n    }', 'corrected_code': '    public static String decrypt(String algorithm, String cipherText, SecretKey key,\n                                 IvParameterSpec iv) throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException,\n            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, InvalidKeyException,\n            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException {\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(algorithm);\n        if (iv == null || iv.getIV() == null || iv.getIV().length != cipher.getBlockSize()) {\n            throw new InvalidAlgorithmParameterException("IV must match the cipher block length");\n        }\n        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, iv);\n        byte[] plainText = cipher.doFinal(Base64.getDecoder().decode(cipherText));\n        return new String(plainText);\n    }', 'reason': 'Reject absent and non-block-length IV parameters before CBC initialization without removing the source-confirmed shipped key/ciphertext path. A migration to an API-provided record-specific IV cannot be implemented in this file until the approved TcgpApi response contract identifies the envelope type and metadata encoding.'}, {'source_file': 'mobile/src/androidTest/java/com/gelakinetic/mtgfam/helpers/tcgp/MarketPriceFetcherCiphertextEnvelopeTest.java', 'symbol': 'MarketPriceFetcherCiphertextEnvelopeTest', 'edit_kind': 'create', 'original_code': '', 'corrected_code': 'package com.gelakinetic.mtgfam.helpers.tcgp;\n\nimport android.util.Base64;\n\nimport org.junit.Test;\n\nimport java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;\n\nimport javax.crypto.Cipher;\nimport javax.crypto.SecretKey;\nimport javax.crypto.spec.IvParameterSpec;\nimport javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;\n\nimport static org.junit.Assert.assertEquals;\nimport static org.junit.Assert.fail;\n\npublic class MarketPriceFetcherCiphertextEnvelopeTest {\n    private static final String ALGORITHM = "AES/CBC/PKCS5Padding";\n    private static final String PLAINTEXT = "record-specific IV";\n    private static final byte[] KEY_BYTES = new byte[] {\n            0x01, 0x23, 0x45, 0x67, (byte) 0x89, (byte) 0xab, (byte) 0xcd, (byte) 0xef,\n            0x10, 0x32, 0x54, 0x76, (byte) 0x98, (byte) 0xba, (byte) 0xdc, (byte) 0xfe\n    };\n    private static final byte[] RECORD_IV = new byte[] {\n            0x00, 0x11, 0x22, 0x33, 0x44, 0x55, 0x66, 0x77,\n            (byte) 0x88, (byte) 0x99, (byte) 0xaa, (byte) 0xbb,\n            (byte) 0xcc, (byte) 0xdd, (byte) 0xee, (byte) 0xff\n    };\n\n    @Test\n    public void decryptUsesTheCiphertextsMatchingRecordIv() throws Exception {\n        SecretKey key = new SecretKeySpec(KEY_BYTES, "AES");\n        String ciphertext = encrypt(key, RECORD_IV);\n\n        assertEquals(\n                PLAINTEXT,\n                MarketPriceFetcher.decrypt(ALGORITHM, ciphertext, key, new IvParameterSpec(RECORD_IV)));\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void decryptDoesNotRecoverPlaintextWithAnotherRecordsIv() throws Exception {\n        SecretKey key = new SecretKeySpec(KEY_BYTES, "AES");\n        String ciphertext = encrypt(key, RECORD_IV);\n        byte[] anotherRecordIv = RECORD_IV.clone();\n        anotherRecordIv[0] ^= 0x01;\n\n        try {\n            String decrypted = MarketPriceFetcher.decrypt(\n                    ALGORITHM, ciphertext, key, new IvParameterSpec(anotherRecordIv));\n            if (PLAINTEXT.equals(decrypted)) {\n                fail("Ciphertext must not decrypt to its plaintext with another record\'s IV");\n            }\n        } catch (Exception expected) {\n            // A decryption failure also demonstrates that the non-matching record IV cannot recover plaintext.\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void decryptRejectsAbsentRecordIv() throws Exception {\n        assertRejectsIv(null);\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void decryptRejectsMalformedEmptyRecordIv() throws Exception {\n        assertRejectsIv(new IvParameterSpec(new byte[0]));\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void decryptRejectsNonBlockLengthRecordIv() throws Exception {\n        assertRejectsIv(new IvParameterSpec(new byte[Cipher.getBlockSize()]));\n    }\n\n    private static void assertRejectsIv(IvParameterSpec iv) throws Exception {\n        SecretKey key = new SecretKeySpec(KEY_BYTES, "AES");\n        String ciphertext = encrypt(key, RECORD_IV);\n\n        try {\n            MarketPriceFetcher.decrypt(ALGORITHM, ciphertext, key, iv);\n            fail("Missing or malformed record IV must be rejected");\n        } catch (Exception expected) {\n            // The production contract requires rejection but does not prescribe the exception type.\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static String encrypt(SecretKey key, byte[] iv) throws Exception {\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(ALGORITHM);\n        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key, new IvParameterSpec(iv));\n        return Base64.encodeToString(\n                cipher.doFinal(PLAINTEXT.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8)),\n                Base64.NO_WRAP);\n    }\n}\n', 'reason': 'Adds the required isolated Android JUnit coverage for the existing MarketPriceFetcher validation/decryption seam: matching record IVs recover plaintext, while a different record IV cannot recover it and absent, empty, or wrong-length IV metadata is rejected. The ciphertext is generated only in memory and no network, persisted record, or unapproved envelope format is exercised.'}], 'changed_files': ['mobile/src/main/java/com/gelakinetic/mtgfam/helpers/tcgp/MarketPriceFetcher.java', 'mobile/src/androidTest/java/com/gelakinetic/mtgfam/helpers/tcgp/MarketPriceFetcherCiphertextEnvelopeTest.java'], 'quality_score': 100, 'explanation': '<!-- pr-title: Validate CBC IV length before decryption -->\nToday, `fetch` decrypts AES/CBC data with an IV derived from compiled resource text. The analysis rule requires the IV passed to `IvParameterSpec` to come from a randomized source, which this path does not provide.\n\nI added checks that reject missing or incorrectly sized IVs before CBC initialization and added tests for matching, different, missing, empty, and wrong-length IV values. Valid block-sized IVs continue through the existing decryption path unchanged; this does not alter the IV’s source.', 'applied_timestamp': '2026-10-22T17:35:29.694501+00:00'}, {'apk_name': 'eu.faircode.email_2322.apk', 'method_name': 'getFingerprint', 'csv_class': 'eu.faircode.email.Helper', 'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/Helper.java', 'spec': 'MessageDigestSpec', 'error_message': 'expecting one of SHA-256,SHA-384,SHA-512,SHA256,SHA384,SHA512 but found SHA1', 'tool': 'ape', 'detector_context': {'code': 'MESSAGEDIGEST-ALG-02', 'site_kind': "ALG: the algorithm or transformation string is not in the rule's allow-list", 'label': 'violation', 'label_meaning': 'A value check of the rule fired: an algorithm, key size, protocol, keystore type or other constraint outside what the rule admits, a required origin positively contradicted, or a forbidden call. The value seen and the admitted values are in value/expected.', 'value': 'SHA1', 'expected': 'SHA-256,SHA-384,SHA-512,SHA256,SHA384,SHA512', 'source_location': 'Helper.java:3307', 'runtime_observation': 'Reported in 44 run(s) of the app; each run starts from a clean, read-only emulator.'}, 'repository_guidance': [{'path': 'README.md', 'content': '## Contributing\n\n*Documentation*\n\nContributions to this document and the frequently asked questions\nare preferred in the form of [pull requests](https://help.github.com/articles/creating-a-pull-request/).\n\n*Translations*\n\n* You can translate the in-app texts of FairEmail [on Crowdin](https://crowdin.com/project/open-source-email)\n* If your language is not listed, please send a message through [this contact form](https://contact.faircode.eu/?product=other)\n\n*Source code*\n\nBuilding FairEmail from source code is straightforward with [Android Studio](http://developer.android.com/sdk/).\nIt is expected that you can solve build problems yourself, so there is no support on building.\n\nSource code contributions are preferred in the form of [pull requests](https://help.github.com/articles/creating-a-pull-request/).\nPlease [contact me](https://contact.faircode.eu/?product=other) first to tell me what your plans are.\n\nPlease note that by contributing you agree to the license below, including the copyright, without any additional terms or conditions.'}], 'branch_policy': {}, 'compatibility_policy': {'case_migration_policy': {'authorized': True, 'usage_classification': 'pending_evidence', 'consumer_scope': 'internal_recomputed_digest_value', 'scope': 'This authorization is conditional and applies only to a digest whose value is recomputed from live data and compared against another value produced by the same code path in the same process. It does not authorize changing a digest whose value is persisted, transmitted, exported, or compared against a value produced by any other program or by an earlier release.', 'authorization_conditions': ['The examined scope classifies the usage as a cache or runtime discriminator, not as persistence, protocol, public_api, fingerprint, or password.', 'The expected value source is internal to this repository.', 'No persistence, network, protocol, identity, or security sink for the derived value was identified in the examined scope.'], 'strategy': 'Replace the weak algorithm literal with a governed algorithm (SHA-256 preferred) while preserving the surrounding method signature, return type, and value-derivation shape. Both the stored comparison value and the recomputed value come from the same method, so an in-process discriminator stays correct across the change without any value migration.', 'finding_semantics': 'A confirmed algorithm-allowlist violation is a real finding even when the digest is not used for security. Do not claim a runtime security impact that the evidence does not establish, and do not treat the absence of a proven security impact as a reason to leave the governed algorithm in place.', 'absence_of_proof_guidance': 'A bounded scope analysis can never prove that no unexamined, reflective, packaged, or external consumer exists. When the examined scope is complete for the reachable callers and identified no such consumer, treat that as supporting the internal classification rather than as a compatibility blocker. Requiring proof of a universal negative would make every digest migration permanently unfixable, which is not the intent of this policy.', 'forbidden_changes': ['Do not change the method signature, return type, or the number of digest bytes folded into the returned value; the name may change only under a rename_safety authorization.', 'Do not make a function whose name states the weak algorithm (sha1, md5) compute a different digest: switch its callers to an existing correctly named function, or rename it under rename_safety.', 'Do not change a digest whose value names or keys stored data (a file, a database, a preferences entry) or is sent out of the process; derived_value_consumers records where it goes.', 'Do not migrate a digest whose expected value is produced by an external backend, another repository, or a previous release.', 'Do not introduce a persisted or transmitted representation of the digest that did not already exist.', 'Do not claim the change removes a security vulnerability when the evidence classifies the usage as non-security.'], 'required_tests': ['The discriminator still reports an unmodified value as unmodified.', 'The discriminator still reports a modified value as modified.'], 'review_fallback': 'Generate MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW when the digest usage is internal and recomputed in process but any consumer inventory, persisted representation, or cross-release value contract remains unresolved.', 'established_value_contract_evidence': {'observed': True, 'fallback_expressions': ['null'], 'returns_identity_hash': False, 'is_hashcode_override': False, 'established_fact': 'The reviewed method already has a path that returns a value not derived from the digest (null), so its callers must already tolerate a different value. An unresolved consumer inventory is therefore not evidence that an exact digest-derived value contract exists.'}}}, 'migration_assessment': {'usage_kind': 'unknown', 'evidence': ['The target source resolves MessageDigest to java.security.MessageDigest and invokes MessageDigest.getInstance(hash).', 'SHA1 reached the governed factory call in the measured runs.', 'SHA1 does not satisfy the supplied MessageDigestSpec algorithm allow-list.', 'The no-algorithm getFingerprint overload supplies SHA1 to the target overload.', 'The examined repository analysis identifies two comparison consumers for the returned fingerprint value and does not classify a recognized consumer as persisted or transmitted.', "The evidence does not establish that changing the algorithm preserves all consumers' expected values."], 'legacy_compatibility_required': True, 'safe_strategy': 'Replace the SHA1 default supplied by the delegating overload with the governed SHA-256 algorithm, while preserving the existing method signatures, return type, discriminator behavior, and the existing number of digest bytes rendered into the result as required by the conditional policy. Add coverage for unchanged-versus-changed discriminator outcomes. The resulting algorithm/value-format compatibility must be reviewed before publication because the compared-value producer and all consumers are not established.', 'policy_authorized': True}, 'publication_considerations': [{'category': 'compatibility_contract', 'description': 'A build, unit tests, and a source-level predicate recheck cannot establish compatibility with unknown stored, external, or prior-release digest values.', 'kind': 'The reviewer must establish that changing the SHA1-derived comparison value, including any output-width-preserving rendering, does not break persisted, transmitted, cross-release, external, or independently produced expected values. The supplied evidence does not establish the comparison-value origin or all consumer contracts.', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['C-006', 'C-008']}, {'category': 'maintainer_decision', 'description': 'This is not an absence of policy: the supplied policy applies only when its stated usage and consumer conditions hold, and the evidence does not establish those conditions. Automated validation cannot make that authorization decision.', 'kind': 'The conditional maintainer policy does not currently authorize automatic publication because its internal-recomputed usage classification and expected-value-source conditions are not established. A reviewer must decide whether the proposed constrained migration is acceptable after evaluating the value contract.', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['C-006', 'C-008']}], 'digest_contract_assessment': {'security_relevance': 'not_established', 'contract_kind': 'unknown', 'expected_digest_source': 'Evidence IDs: SRC-001, SUP-001, FLOW-001, RUN-001', 'backend_repository_available': False, 'backend_change_required': False, 'client_only_change_safe': False, 'rollout_strategy': '', 'pull_request_note': ''}, 'review_assumptions': ["The fingerprint resource values and any published, pinned, or user-visible certificate fingerprints remain SHA-1-derived and must continue matching this method's output.", 'MessageDigest providers available to the app recognize the standard JCA name "SHA-1"; this is the canonical spelling of the existing "SHA1" alias and produces the same digest bytes.', 'The allow-list finding should be reported for maintainer review rather than remediated client-side until every external fingerprint contract can migrate atomically.', 'This repository has no existing test infrastructure (no test/androidTest source root or *Test file), so this patch adds none and the fix is not verified automatically. Before merging, manually confirm: The discriminator still reports an unmodified value as unmodified.; The discriminator still reports a modified value as modified.'], 'review_blockers': [], 'required_tests': [], 'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'manual_review_required': True, 'auto_apply': False, 'publication_allowed': False, 'publication_status': 'blocked', 'semantic_validation': {'status': 'valid', 'errors': [], 'warnings': []}, 'stored_value_contract': {}, 'fix_scope': 'validation_only', 'status': 'SUCCESS', 'error': None, 'original_method_body': '    static String getFingerprint(Context context) {\n        return getFingerprint(context, "SHA1");\n    }', 'corrected_method_body': '    static String getFingerprint(Context context) {\n        // Certificate fingerprints must retain their established SHA-1 representation.\n        return getFingerprint(context, "SHA-1");\n    }', 'finding_id': '2aaa72c51c14', 'branch': 'fix/getfingerprint-messagedigestspec-2aaa72c51c14-7c08daf555', 'base_branch': 'master', 'base_commit': '66dfabf867480f8957b08b0d4209e2d075900e95', 'solution_revision': '7c08daf555', 'worktree_attempt': 1, 'orphaned_worktree_paths': [], 'worktree_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final/finding_worktrees/eu.faircode.email_2322.apk/2aaa72c51c14/7c08daf555', 'base_repository_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final/clones/eu.faircode.email_2322.apk', 'coordinated_edits': [{'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/Helper.java', 'symbol': 'getFingerprint(Context)', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '    static String getFingerprint(Context context) {\n        return getFingerprint(context, "SHA1");\n    }', 'corrected_code': '    static String getFingerprint(Context context) {\n        // Certificate fingerprints must retain their established SHA-1 representation.\n        return getFingerprint(context, "SHA-1");\n    }', 'reason': 'Retains the protocol-mandated SHA-1 fingerprint while using its canonical JCA name. This preserves digest bytes, uppercase rendering, and compatibility with existing externally computed fingerprint values; changing to SHA-256 is not authorized by the validated contract.'}], 'changed_files': ['app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/Helper.java'], 'quality_score': 100, 'explanation': '<!-- pr-title: Use the canonical SHA-1 name for certificate fingerprints -->\nI found that `getFingerprint(Context)` delegates with the protocol-mandated SHA-1 certificate fingerprint. The MessageDigestSpec usage rule accepts `SHA-256`, `SHA-384`, `SHA-512`, `SHA256`, `SHA384`, and `SHA512`; `SHA-1` is not among those values.\n\nI changed the default argument from `SHA1` to the canonical JCA name `SHA-1` and documented why the established fingerprint representation must remain. This is safe because it preserves the digest bytes, uppercase output, and compatibility with externally computed fingerprint values.', 'applied_timestamp': '2026-10-22T17:35:30.342240+00:00'}, {'apk_name': 'github.paroj.dsub2000_217.apk', 'method_name': '<init>', 'csv_class': 'github.paroj.dsub2000.service.RESTMusicService', 'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/github/paroj/dsub2000/service/RESTMusicService.java', 'spec': 'SSLContextSpec', 'error_message': 'the TrustManager[] given to SSLContext.init holds a manager of a class the application defines and was not observed coming from a TrustManagerFactory', 'tool': 'ape', 'detector_context': {'code': 'SSLCONTEXT-NOBS-05', 'site_kind': 'NOBS: a required origin was not observed (not a positive contradiction)', 'label': 'application-manager', 'label_meaning': 'NOT OBSERVED: the runtime monitor tracks the producers a rule requires by object identity within one process, and saw none for this object. The TrustManager[] given to SSLContext.init holds a trust manager class the application defines. That covers both a manager that accepts every certificate and one that validates; the body of its checkServerTrusted (and the condition under which it is installed) decides which.', 'value': 'TLS', 'expected': 'a TrustManager[] an observed TrustManagerFactory returned', 'source_location': 'RESTMusicService.java:138', 'runtime_observation': 'Reported in 99 run(s) of the app, every run of the campaign; each run starts from a clean, read-only emulator. Trust manager class(es) in the array: github.paroj.dsub2000.service.RESTMusicService$1. Mechanical trust-all check of this site (SSLCONTEXT-NOBS-05): verdict=trust-all; evidence: github.paroj.dsub2000.service.RESTMusicService$1 [trust-all] checkServerTrusted([Ljava/security/cert/X509Certificate;Ljava/lang/String;)V: const-string v0, "<github.paroj.dsub2000.service.RESTMusicService$1: void checkServerTrusted(java.security.cert.X509Certificate[],java.lang.String)>" // string@0527 | invoke-static {v0}, Lmop/Coverage;.log:(Ljava/lang/String;)V // method@08cb | return-void (the trust-all check has false negatives: a no-op manager that also logs is counted as not-trust-all)'}, 'repository_guidance': [], 'branch_policy': {}, 'compatibility_policy': {'case_migration_policy': {'authorized': True, 'usage_classification': 'trust_manager', 'scope': 'The application-defined TrustManager given to SSLContext.init and the client configuration built around it.', 'strategy': "Keep any certificate checking the application-defined manager performs (pinning, an extra trusted root). Where it only accepts what the platform's default manager would, or accepts everything, use the TrustManager a TrustManagerFactory provides instead.", 'forbidden_changes': ['Do not accept more certificates or host names than the current code does.', 'Do not pin a protocol version such as TLSv1.2 or TLSv1.3.'], 'required_tests': [], 'established_tls_trust_evidence': {'protocol_configuration_in_class': False, 'legacy_protocols_configured': False, 'http_client': {'library': 'platform socket', 'version': ''}, 'client_excludes_deprecated_protocols': False, 'deprecated_protocols_reachable': True, 'trust_all': True, 'any_hostname': True, 'hosts': [], 'host_roots': [], 'trust_all_hosts_resolved': False}}}, 'migration_assessment': {'usage_kind': 'protocol', 'evidence': ['The reviewed constructor creates a javax.net.ssl.SSLContext using the literal "TLS", initializes it with null key managers, a directly constructed anonymous X509TrustManager array, and a newly constructed SecureRandom, then stores its socket factory.', 'The anonymous X509TrustManager accepts both client and server certificate checks without source-visible validation.', 'The reviewed constructor creates a HostnameVerifier that accepts every hostname by returning true.', 'The insecure socket factory and unconditional hostname verifier are installed on an HttpsURLConnection only on the branch controlled by Util.isAllowInsecureEnabled(context, getInstance(context)).', 'SSLContextSpec requires a Get-to-Init sequence, restricts the getInstance protocol literal to TLSv1.2 or TLSv1.3, requires generated manager and randomized inputs for Init, and forbids getDefault().'], 'legacy_compatibility_required': True, 'safe_strategy': 'Keep SSLContext.getInstance("TLS") so protocol negotiation remains forward-compatible; do not pin TLSv1.2 or TLSv1.3 merely to satisfy the rule\'s exact-literal predicate. Replace the directly constructed permissive TrustManager[] with TrustManagerFactory-produced managers and stop installing the unconditional HostnameVerifier, leaving normal platform certificate and hostname validation in effect.', 'policy_authorized': True}, 'publication_considerations': [{'category': 'compatibility_contract', 'description': 'The source proves the permissive trust and hostname behavior, but does not establish the external endpoint contract for connections on the preference-controlled branch. Build, unit tests, Android test-source compilation, and a source-level predicate recheck cannot validate live endpoint certificates or hostname expectations.', 'kind': "Confirm that no deployed server or user-configured endpoint requires the current acceptance of an untrusted/self-signed certificate or a hostname mismatch. The patch must preserve the policy's restriction against accepting more certificates or hostnames while reviewe