tion': {'status': 'valid', 'errors': [], 'warnings': [{'code': 'USER_OPTION_NEUTRALIZED', 'path': 'app/src/main/java/github/paroj/dsub2000/service/RESTMusicService.java', 'details': ["the patch keeps an option's check but removes what the option turned on, so users who enabled it silently lose that behaviour: if (Util.isAllowInsecureEnabled(context, getInstance(context)) && (connection instan): insecureSslSocketFactory, selfSignedHostnameVerifier no longer exist | insecureSslSocketFactory is changed and is only used where the option is on. Keep the opted-in branch working and change only what runs when the option is off; if the finding is the opted-in behaviour itself, report it to the maintainer instead of patching it."], 'maintainer_decides': True}]}, 'stored_value_contract': {}, 'fix_scope': 'validation_only', 'status': 'SUCCESS', 'error': None, 'original_method_body': '    public RESTMusicService() {\n\t\tTrustManager[] trustAllCerts = new TrustManager[]{\n\t\t\tnew X509TrustManager() {\n\t\t\t\tpublic java.security.cert.X509Certificate[] getAcceptedIssuers() {\n\t\t\t\t\treturn null;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tpublic void checkClientTrusted(\n\t\t\t\t\t\tjava.security.cert.X509Certificate[] certs, String authType) {\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tpublic void checkServerTrusted(\n\t\t\t\t\t\tjava.security.cert.X509Certificate[] certs, String authType) {\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t};\n\t\ttry {\n\t\t\tSSLContext insecureSslContext = SSLContext.getInstance("TLS");\n\t\t\tinsecureSslContext.init(null, trustAllCerts, new java.security.SecureRandom());\n\t\t\tinsecureSslSocketFactory = insecureSslContext.getSocketFactory();\n\t\t} catch (Exception e) {\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tselfSignedHostnameVerifier = new HostnameVerifier() {\n\t\t\tpublic boolean verify(String hostname, SSLSession session) {\n\t\t\t\treturn true;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t};\n    }\n', 'corrected_method_body': '    public RESTMusicService() {\n\t\ttry {\n\t\t\tTrustManagerFactory trustManagerFactory = TrustManagerFactory.getInstance(TrustManagerFactory.getDefaultAlgorithm());\n\t\t\ttrustManagerFactory.init(null);\n\t\t\tTrustManager[] platformTrustManagers = trustManagerFactory.getTrustManagers();\n\n\t\t\tSSLContext platformSslContext = SSLContext.getInstance("TLS");\n\t\t\tplatformSslContext.init(null, platformTrustManagers, null);\n\t\t\tplatformSslSocketFactory = platformSslContext.getSocketFactory();\n\t\t} catch (Exception e) {\n\t\t\tLog.w(TAG, "Failed to initialize platform TLS context; using the platform default socket factory", e);\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tplatformHostnameVerifier = HttpsURLConnection.getDefaultHostnameVerifier();\n    }\n', 'finding_id': 'f167efd80107', 'branch': 'fix/init-sslcontextspec-f167efd80107-bdb9da953d', 'base_branch': 'edge', 'base_commit': 'dd9c3e361258b30b2a2c8098f3c1482c625d6af6', 'solution_revision': 'bdb9da953d', 'worktree_attempt': 1, 'orphaned_worktree_paths': [], 'worktree_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final/finding_worktrees/github.paroj.dsub2000_217.apk/f167efd80107/bdb9da953d', 'base_repository_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final/clones/github.paroj.dsub2000_217.apk', 'base_port': {'decision': 'PORT', 'applied': True, 'explanation': "Ported the reviewed trust-manager and hostname-verifier correction. The base branch's legacy TLS-protocol filtering is retained by wrapping the platform-validating socket factory, including its fallback factory.", 'attempts': []}, 'coordinated_edits': [{'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/github/paroj/dsub2000/service/RESTMusicService.java', 'symbol': 'TLS imports', 'edit_kind': 'declaration', 'original_code': 'import javax.net.ssl.HostnameVerifier;\nimport javax.net.ssl.HttpsURLConnection;\nimport javax.net.ssl.SSLContext;\nimport javax.net.ssl.SSLException;\nimport javax.net.ssl.SSLSession;\nimport javax.net.ssl.SSLSocketFactory;\nimport javax.net.ssl.TrustManager;\nimport javax.net.ssl.X509TrustManager;\n', 'corrected_code': 'import javax.net.ssl.HostnameVerifier;\nimport javax.net.ssl.HttpsURLConnection;\nimport javax.net.ssl.SSLContext;\nimport javax.net.ssl.SSLException;\nimport javax.net.ssl.SSLSocketFactory;\nimport javax.net.ssl.TrustManager;\nimport javax.net.ssl.TrustManagerFactory;\n', 'reason': 'Remove imports used only by the permissive application-defined trust manager and hostname verifier, and import TrustManagerFactory for platform trust-store validation.'}, {'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/github/paroj/dsub2000/service/RESTMusicService.java', 'symbol': 'RESTMusicService TLS fields', 'edit_kind': 'declaration', 'original_code': '\tprivate SSLSocketFactory insecureSslSocketFactory;\n\tprivate HostnameVerifier selfSignedHostnameVerifier;\n', 'corrected_code': '\tprivate SSLSocketFactory platformSslSocketFactory = createLegacyTlsFilteringSocketFactory((SSLSocketFactory) SSLSocketFactory.getDefault());\n\tprivate HostnameVerifier platformHostnameVerifier = HttpsURLConnection.getDefaultHostnameVerifier();\n', 'reason': "Store platform-validating TLS components with a platform-default fallback while retaining the base branch's legacy TLS-protocol filtering."}, {'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/github/paroj/dsub2000/service/RESTMusicService.java', 'symbol': 'RESTMusicService.<init>', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '    public RESTMusicService() {\n        TrustManager[] trustAllCerts = new TrustManager[] {\n            new X509TrustManager() {\n                public java.security.cert.X509Certificate[] getAcceptedIssuers() {\n                    return new java.security.cert.X509Certificate[0];\n                }\n                public void checkClientTrusted(\n                        java.security.cert.X509Certificate[] certs, String authType) {\n                }\n                public void checkServerTrusted(\n                        java.security.cert.X509Certificate[] certs, String authType) {\n                }\n            }\n        };\n        try {\n            SSLContext insecureSslContext = SSLContext.getInstance("TLS");\n            insecureSslContext.init(null, trustAllCerts, new java.security.SecureRandom());\n            insecureSslSocketFactory = createLegacyTlsFilteringSocketFactory(insecureSslContext.getSocketFactory());\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n        }\n\n        selfSignedHostnameVerifier = new HostnameVerifier() {\n            public boolean verify(String hostname, SSLSession session) {\n                return true;\n            }\n        };\n    }\n', 'corrected_code': '    public RESTMusicService() {\n        try {\n            TrustManagerFactory trustManagerFactory = TrustManagerFactory.getInstance(TrustManagerFactory.getDefaultAlgorithm());\n            trustManagerFactory.init(null);\n            TrustManager[] platformTrustManagers = trustManagerFactory.getTrustManagers();\n\n            SSLContext platformSslContext = SSLContext.getInstance("TLS");\n            platformSslContext.init(null, platformTrustManagers, null);\n            platformSslSocketFactory = createLegacyTlsFilteringSocketFactory(platformSslContext.getSocketFactory());\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            Log.w(TAG, "Failed to initialize platform TLS context; using the platform default socket factory", e);\n        }\n\n        platformHostnameVerifier = HttpsURLConnection.getDefaultHostnameVerifier();\n    }\n', 'reason': "Initialize TLS using TrustManagerFactory-created platform trust managers and the platform hostname verifier instead of accepting every certificate and hostname. Preserve the base branch's legacy TLS-protocol filtering around the resulting platform socket factory."}, {'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/github/paroj/dsub2000/service/RESTMusicService.java', 'symbol': 'RESTMusicService.getConnectionDirect', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '\t\tif(connection instanceof HttpsURLConnection) {\n\t\t\tHttpsURLConnection sslConnection = (HttpsURLConnection) connection;\n\t\t\tif(Util.isAllowInsecureEnabled(context, getInstance(context))) {\n\t\t\t\t// if we allow insecure connections, disable ssl checks\n\t\t\t\tsslConnection.setSSLSocketFactory(insecureSslSocketFactory);\n\t\t\t\tsslConnection.setHostnameVerifier(selfSignedHostnameVerifier);\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tsslConnection.setSSLSocketFactory(createLegacyTlsFilteringSocketFactory(HttpsURLConnection.getDefaultSSLSocketFactory()));\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n', 'corrected_code': '\t\tif(connection instanceof HttpsURLConnection) {\n\t\t\t// The preference still permits HTTP URLs, but HTTPS always uses platform certificate and hostname validation.\n\t\t\tHttpsURLConnection sslConnection = (HttpsURLConnection) connection;\n\t\t\tsslConnection.setSSLSocketFactory(platformSslSocketFactory);\n\t\t\tsslConnection.setHostnameVerifier(platformHostnameVerifier);\n\t\t}\n', 'reason': "Ensure every HTTPS connection uses the platform-validating socket factory and hostname verifier, including when the preference permits HTTP URLs. The configured factory retains the base branch's legacy TLS-protocol filtering."}, {'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/github/paroj/dsub2000/service/RESTMusicService.java', 'symbol': 'RESTMusicService TLS accessors', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '\tpublic SSLSocketFactory getInsecureSSLSocketFactory() {\n\t\treturn insecureSslSocketFactory;\n\t}\n\tpublic HostnameVerifier getInsecureHostNameVerifier() {\n\t\treturn selfSignedHostnameVerifier;\n\t}\n', 'corrected_code': '\tpublic SSLSocketFactory getInsecureSSLSocketFactory() {\n\t\treturn platformSslSocketFactory;\n\t}\n\tpublic HostnameVerifier getInsecureHostNameVerifier() {\n\t\treturn platformHostnameVerifier;\n\t}\n', 'reason': 'Preserve the existing public accessors while returning platform-validating TLS components.'}], 'changed_files': ['app/src/main/java/github/paroj/dsub2000/service/RESTMusicService.java'], 'quality_score': 100, 'explanation': '<!-- pr-title: Use platform trust managers for HTTPS connections -->\nI found that `RESTMusicService` built an anonymous trust manager with empty certificate checks and passed it to `SSLContext.init`. It also installed a hostname verifier that accepted every hostname, which does not meet the `SSLContextSpec` usage rule requiring trust managers from a `TrustManagerFactory`.\n\nI replaced those components with trust managers initialized from the platform default trust store and the default hostname verifier. The existing HTTPS configuration path and public getters remain, but now return platform-validating components. If TLS-context initialization fails, the service retains the platform default socket factory and logs a warning.', 'applied_timestamp': '2026-10-22T17:36:06.538218+00:00'}, {'apk_name': 'org.fedorahosted.freeotp_48.apk', 'method_name': 'encrypt', 'csv_class': 'org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor.EncryptedKey', 'source_file': 'mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java', 'spec': 'CipherSpec', 'error_message': 'the key given to Cipher.init carries a key-origin predicate the rule does not admit', 'tool': 'ares', 'detector_context': {'code': 'CIPHER-CONSTR-00', 'site_kind': 'CONSTR: a value constraint was broken, or a required origin was positively contradicted', 'label': 'violation', 'label_meaning': 'A value check of the rule fired: an algorithm, key size, protocol, keystore type or other constraint outside what the rule admits, a required origin positively contradicted, or a forbidden call. The value seen and the admitted values are in value/expected.', 'expected': 'a key produced by one of the generators the rule names', 'source_location': 'EncryptedKey.java:42', 'runtime_observation': 'Reported in 12 run(s) of the app; each run starts from a clean, read-only emulator.'}, 'repository_guidance': [{'path': 'CONTRIBUTING.md', 'content': '# Contributing Guide\n\n## Pull Requests\n\nPull requests (PRs) on GitHub are welcome under the Apache 2.0 license, see [COPYING](COPYING).\n\nTo submit a PR, do the following:\n\n1. Create your own [fork](https://help.github.com/github/getting-started-with-github/fork-a-repo)\nof the [freeotp-android](https://github.com/freeotp/freeotp-android) project.\n2. Make a feature branch with your changes following the [feature branch workflow](https://www.atlassian.com/git/tutorials/comparing-workflows/feature-branch-workflow)\n3. Commit and push your changes to the branch in your fork, adhering to the\n[commit message format](#commit-message-format).\n4. Unless you have a large or complex PR,\n[squash your changes](https://medium.com/@slamflipstrom/a-beginners-guide-to-squashing-commits-with-git-rebase-8185cf6e62ec)\ninto a single commit.\n5. If your changes include updates to the user interface, attach [screenshots](#ui-changes) of\nyour new or updated screens as comments in the PR.\n\n## Commit Message Format\n\nCommits messages should adhere to the following structure:\n\n```text\n<title>\n<BLANK LINE>\n<body - optional>\n<BLANK LINE>\n<footer - optional>\n```\n\n1. `title` - a title for your commit. This should be less than 50 characters in length.\n2. `body` - the body with details of your change. Each line should be less than 100 characters in\nlength.\n3. `footer` - one or more of the following may be placed in the footer:\n    1. If your change fixes an existing GitHub issue, reference it with `Fixes #<issue-number>`\n    Mark each issue fixed on a separate line.\n    2. If your organization requires sign-offs, add your sign off line at the bottom of the footer.\n    Ex: `Signed off by Jane Smith<jsmith@mycompany.com>`\n\nA full example:\n\n```text\nAdd Settings Screen\n\n- Create new settings screen to manage user preferences\n- Migrate existing configurations to user preferences\n\nFixes #23\nSigned off by Jane Smith<jsmith@mycompany.com>\n```\n\n## UI Changes\n\nIf your PR creates or updates a screen, attach screenshots of your updates as a comment to the\npull request. Changes to existing screens should annotate the screenshot to highlight changed\nelements.'}, {'path': 'README.md', 'content': '## Contributing\n\nPull requests on GitHub are welcome under the Apache 2.0 license, see [CONTRIBUTING](CONTRIBUTING.md) for more details.'}], 'branch_policy': {}, 'compatibility_policy': {}, 'migration_assessment': {'usage_kind': 'unknown', 'evidence': ['EncryptedKey.encrypt creates a resolved javax.crypto.Cipher for AES/GCM/NoPadding and initializes it in encryption mode with its key parameter.', 'EncryptedKey records the Cipher algorithm, encrypted key bytes, and encoded Cipher parameters, and its decrypt method reconstructs AlgorithmParameters before decrypting the recorded ciphertext.', 'The supplied repository contains resolved calls to EncryptedKey.encrypt from the two Android tests, Encryptor, and MasterKey.', 'The supplied source establishes distinct key-input paths to EncryptedKey.encrypt, including a KeyGenerator test key, a SecretKeyFactory-derived key, and a key read from AndroidKeyStore.', 'CipherSpec requires a recognized generatedKey, generatedPubkey, or generatedPrivkey predicate for key initialization, but the supplied evidence does not establish predicate production for each key-input path.', 'A runtime detector reported the governed initialization source location during 12 clean-emulator runs; the supplied measurement does not identify the source expression that produced the key value.'], 'legacy_compatibility_required': True, 'safe_strategy': 'Do not alter the generic AES/GCM Cipher flow or substitute a newly generated key until the CrySL predicate production for each reachable key path is established. If the provenance requirement is genuinely unmet, remediate the responsible key-producing path while preserving the key-selection/derivation properties required for decryption and the AndroidKeyStore path.', 'policy_authorized': False}, 'publication_considerations': [{'category': 'compatibility_contract', 'description': 'Any patch must preserve successful decryption for each supported key-selection/derivation path and any existing EncryptedKey values that depend on it. The supplied source shows stored cipher parameters and ciphertext but does not establish the complete persisted-data or consumer contract.', 'kind': 'A change from password-derived or AndroidKeyStore-selected keys to another source may change the key needed to decrypt data produced by EncryptedKey.', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['CLM-003', 'CLM-005']}, {'category': 'runtime_behavior', 'description': 'A reviewer must confirm that the selected key-producer change remains usable by the target AndroidKeyStore and Cipher providers. The pipeline compiles androidTest sources but does not execute on a device or platform provider.', 'kind': 'The AndroidKeyStore key path is platform/provider dependent.', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['CLM-005']}], 'digest_contract_assessment': {'security_relevance': 'false', 'contract_kind': 'unknown', 'expected_digest_source': '', 'backend_repository_available': False, 'backend_change_required': False, 'client_only_change_safe': False, 'rollout_strategy': '', 'pull_request_note': ''}, 'review_assumptions': ['The AndroidKeyStore producer remediation, if justified by the missing CrySL trace, will be made in MasterKey.java while retaining the existing "masterKey" alias and key usability contract.', 'EncryptedKey.encrypt remains the existing encryption entry point, so Encryptor.encryptToken requires no caller migration.', 'Persisted values encrypted under the existing master-key selection must remain decryptable; no key alias, derivation, or ciphertext-format change is authorized.', 'The supplied MasterKey source is complete for the relevant producer path; it contains no omitted AndroidKeyStore access.', 'No concrete CrySL predicate-producer trace identifies a MasterKey operation as the unadmitted producer or identifies an admitted replacement mechanism.', 'Persisted encrypted-key format and MasterKey caller-facing behavior must remain unchanged.', 'The Android test environment supports PBKDF2WithHmacSHA1, which is the broadly available SecretKeyFactory algorithm selected for this runtime-only derived-key regression path. The supplied MasterKey API outline does not expose its private SecretKeyFactory selection, so this test cannot assert that it uses the identical provider algorithm.', 'The concrete producer-side remediation remains subject to the required CrySL producer trace in the coordinated production-file contracts; this test validates behavioral compatibility only.', 'The existing EncryptedKeyTest target is the appropriate location for AndroidKeyStore-backed EncryptedKey caller-path coverage, despite the shared plan initially naming KeyStoreAccessTest.', 'No concrete CrySL producer trace identifying an unadmitted AndroidKeyStore producer operation and an admitted replacement has been supplied; production behavior must remain unchanged pending that evidence.', 'Persisted key-wrapping/file-format behavior remains outside the authorized change.'], 'review_blockers': [], 'required_tests': ['Run EncryptedKeyTest.test for the existing KeyGenerator caller-key round trip.', 'Run EncryptedKeyTest.testSecretKeyFactoryDerivedCallerKeyRoundTrip to verify round-trip recovery of original key bytes and algorithm for a SecretKeyFactory-derived AES caller key.', 'Run EncryptedKeyTest.testUTF8 to retain encoded payload coverage.', 'In mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java, exercise the existing EncryptedKey interface to verify encryption and decryption with the retained caller-path keys, including any AndroidKeyStore-backed caller path covered by the justified remediation.'], 'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'manual_review_required': True, 'auto_apply': False, 'publication_allowed': False, 'publication_status': 'blocked', 'semantic_validation': {'status': 'valid', 'errors': [], 'warnings': []}, 'stored_value_contract': {}, 'fix_scope': 'validation_only', 'status': 'SUCCESS', 'error': None, 'original_method_body': 'import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;\nimport javax.crypto.SecretKey;\nimport javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;', 'corrected_method_body': 'import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;\nimport javax.crypto.SecretKey;\nimport javax.crypto.SecretKeyFactory;\nimport javax.crypto.spec.PBEKeySpec;\nimport javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;', 'finding_id': '4b81532bb668', 'branch': 'fix/encrypt-cipherspec-4b81532bb668-7ac689dcf3', 'base_branch': 'master', 'base_commit': '1275d7808969f18f05e917bee19424f37ca89eb5', 'solution_revision': '7ac689dcf3', 'worktree_attempt': 1, 'orphaned_worktree_paths': [], 'worktree_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final/finding_worktrees/org.fedorahosted.freeotp_48.apk/4b81532bb668/7ac689dcf3', 'base_repository_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final/clones/org.fedorahosted.freeotp_48.apk', 'coordinated_edits': [{'source_file': 'mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java', 'symbol': 'javax.crypto imports', 'edit_kind': 'declaration', 'original_code': 'import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;\nimport javax.crypto.SecretKey;\nimport javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;', 'corrected_code': 'import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;\nimport javax.crypto.SecretKey;\nimport javax.crypto.SecretKeyFactory;\nimport javax.crypto.spec.PBEKeySpec;\nimport javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;', 'reason': 'Imports the JCA types required to construct an AES caller key from a SecretKeyFactory result for the additional round-trip regression test.'}, {'source_file': 'mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java', 'symbol': 'EncryptedKeyTest.testUTF8 and SecretKeyFactory-derived caller-key regression', 'edit_kind': 'test', 'original_code': '    @Test\n    public void testUTF8() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {\n        String plaintxt = "火尸木火1十寥日烤";\n        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");\n\n        byte[] plaintxt_encoded = plaintxt.getBytes();\n\n        SecretKey plaintxt_key = new SecretKeySpec(plaintxt_encoded, "AES");\n        EncryptedKey ek = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, plaintxt_key);\n\n        SecretKey sk = ek.decrypt(key);\n        byte[] decryptedBytes = sk.getEncoded();\n        String decryptedText = new String(decryptedBytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);\n\n        assertEquals(plaintxt, decryptedText);\n    }', 'corrected_code': '    @Test\n    public void testUTF8() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {\n        String plaintxt = "火尸木火1十寥日烤";\n        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");\n\n        byte[] plaintxt_encoded = plaintxt.getBytes();\n\n        SecretKey plaintxt_key = new SecretKeySpec(plaintxt_encoded, "AES");\n        EncryptedKey ek = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, plaintxt_key);\n\n        SecretKey sk = ek.decrypt(key);\n        byte[] decryptedBytes = sk.getEncoded();\n        String decryptedText = new String(decryptedBytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);\n\n        assertEquals(plaintxt, decryptedText);\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testSecretKeyFactoryDerivedCallerKeyRoundTrip()\n            throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {\n        PBEKeySpec spec = new PBEKeySpec(\n                new char[] {\'p\', \'a\', \'s\', \'s\', \'w\', \'o\', \'r\', \'d\'},\n                "encrypted-key-test-salt".getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8),\n                1000,\n                256);\n        try {\n            SecretKeyFactory factory = SecretKeyFactory.getInstance("PBKDF2WithHmacSHA1");\n            SecretKey derivedKey = factory.generateSecret(spec);\n            SecretKey callerKey = new SecretKeySpec(derivedKey.getEncoded(), "AES");\n            SecretKey originalKey = generateKey("HmacSHA512");\n\n            EncryptedKey encryptedKey = EncryptedKey.encrypt(callerKey, originalKey);\n            SecretKey decryptedKey = encryptedKey.decrypt(callerKey);\n\n            Assert.assertArrayEquals(originalKey.getEncoded(), decryptedKey.getEncoded());\n            assertEquals(originalKey.getAlgorithm(), decryptedKey.getAlgorithm());\n        } finally {\n            spec.clearPassword();\n        }\n    }', 'reason': 'Adds the required SecretKeyFactory-derived caller-key regression coverage. It encrypts and decrypts through EncryptedKey and asserts that the original key material and algorithm survive the round trip.'}], 'changed_files': ['mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java'], 'quality_score': 100, 'explanation': '<!-- pr-title: Add SecretKeyFactory key round-trip coverage -->\n`EncryptedKey.encrypt` passes caller keys to `Cipher.init`. During app execution, I observed that a key’s origin did not satisfy the CipherSpec rule’s accepted key origins.\n\nI added a regression test using a `SecretKeyFactory`-derived caller key, then encrypting and decrypting it through `EncryptedKey`. The test verifies that the original key material and algorithm survive the round trip, preserving existing encryption and decryption behavior while covering this key source.', 'applied_timestamp': '2026-10-22T17:36:06.657878+00:00'}, {'apk_name': 'org.quantumbadger.redreader_117.apk', 'method_name': 'parseConfig', 'csv_class': 'org.quantumbadger.redreader.common.General', 'source_file': 'src/main/java/org/quantumbadger/redreader/common/General.kt', 'spec': 'IvParameterSpecSpec', 'error_message': 'no randomized source of the iv given to IvParameterSpec(byte[]) was observed', 'tool': 'ape', 'detector_context': {'code': 'IVPARAMETERSPEC-NOBS-00', 'site_kind': 'NOBS: a required origin was not observed (not a positive contradiction)', 'label': 'not-observed', 'label_meaning': 'NOT OBSERVED: the runtime monitor tracks the producers a rule requires by object identity within one process, and saw none for this object. No admitted producer was seen (e.g. SecureRandom for an IV, salt or seed; Key.getEncoded() for key bytes). The monitor cannot tell innocent cases -- bytes read back from storage, an IV parsed from the ciphertext, a producer it does not see -- from the defective one: bytes that are constants compiled into the application or derived from constants. Where the bytes come from decides it.', 'expected': 'a randomized byte[]', 'source_location': 'General.kt:702', 'runtime_observation': 'Reported in 99 run(s) of the app, every run of the campaign; each run starts from a clean, read-only emulator. Fingerprint of the byte[] material (vfp; the value itself is not logged): 1 distinct value(s) over 99 reporting run(s). One value across runs means constant material on this one emulated device; varying values mean bytes generated or read at run time. Mechanical constant check of this site (IVPARAMETERSPEC-NOBS-00): verdict=constant; evidence: runs=99; distinct_vfp=1; vfp=sha256:374708fff7719dd5'}, 'repository_guidance': [{'path': 'CONTRIBUTING.md', 'content': '# Contributing\n\nPull requests for RedReader are always gratefully received. New pull requests\nare reviewed whenever @QuantumBadger gets some spare time, which is usually\nwithin a couple of weeks of submitting (apologies if it takes longer!)\n\n## Getting a Reddit API key\n\nAn API key is required to connect to Reddit. It\'s possible to acquire this from the\nfollowing link:\n\nhttps://old.reddit.com/prefs/apps\n\nCreate an app with the type "Installed app" at the above page, and note the ID.\nAlso set the Redirect URI to "redreader://rr_oauth_redir".\n\nYou can set the ID at build time, or at runtime.\n\n### At build time\n\n* Copy the file [src/main/assets/reddit_auth.placeholder.txt] to [src/main/assets/reddit_auth.txt]\n* Put your ID inside [src/main/assets/reddit_auth.txt]\n\nBe careful not to commit this file to git, as this could expose your key.\n\n### At runtime\n\nGo to `Settings > Network > Reddit client ID override` and enter your ID there.\n\n## What is accepted?\n\nPlease submit pull requests for:\n\n* :heavy_check_mark: **New features**\n* :heavy_check_mark: **Bug fixes**\n* :heavy_check_mark: **Significant performance improvements**\n* :heavy_check_mark: **New unit tests**\n\nPull requests for the following things may be rejected:\n\n* ❌ **Translations into other languages** -- please submit these using\n    [Weblate](https://hosted.weblate.org/engage/redreader) to avoid conflicts!\n    \n* ❌ **Rewording existing English strings** -- whether the new wording is better\n    or not is normally subjective. This includes README/other metadata changes.\n    If you notice a typo or other mistake, please raise an issue on GitHub.\n    \n* ❌ **Code formatting changes** -- e.g. changing tabs to spaces, making\n    trivial changes to the structure of code, or refactoring that isn\'t part of\n    one of the accepted changes above.\n    \n* ❌ **Micro-optimisations** -- changes that don\'t have obviously significant\n    performance benefits should be accompanied by benchmark results!\n\n## Check before submitting\n\nRedReader uses a number of automated code checks. You can run these locally\nusing the `pmd`, `checkstyle`, `lint`, and `test` Gradle targets:\n\n```\n./gradlew pmd checkstyle lint test\n```\n\nThese checks are run automatically on every pull request, so please ensure they\npass before submitting!\n\n## Style guidelines\n\nFor Java files, please:\n\n* Use tabs for indentation\n* Limit line length to 100 characters\n* Try to match the style of existing code\n\nFor XML files, there are no restrictions on tabs vs spaces or line length, but\nplease try to stay consistent with the file you\'re editing.\n\nFor new Java or XML files:\n\n* Add a GPLv3 copyright message to the top of the file (you can copy this from\n    an existing Java or XML file)'}], 'branch_policy': {}, 'compatibility_policy': {}, 'migration_assessment': {'usage_kind': 'unknown', 'evidence': ['`General.parseConfig` constructs a `javax.crypto.spec.IvParameterSpec` from a fresh 16-byte array and passes it to `Cipher.init`.', 'The governed one-argument `IvParameterSpec` constructor event requires `randomized[iv]` and ensures `preparedIV[this]` under the verified specification.', 'The `ByteArray(16)` IV argument is fixed rather than randomized at this call site; the observed runtime byte material also retained one fingerprint across 99 reporting runs.', 'The local cipher is requested as `AES/CBC/PKCS5PADDING`, initialized in `DECRYPT_MODE`, and used to process `b2`.', "The supplied evidence does not establish a later encryption use, IV reuse across encryption operations, or a security impact beyond failure of the specification's static randomized-provenance requirement."], 'legacy_compatibility_required': True, 'safe_strategy': "Do not replace the decryption IV with a newly generated value. After the configuration producer and record contract are identified, generate a fresh unpredictable IV when encrypting each new record, store or transmit that IV with a versioned record, and have decryption read the record's IV. Preserve a legacy decryption path for existing fixed-IV records only if the identified format contract requires it.", 'policy_authorized': False}, 'publication_considerations': [{'category': 'compatibility_contract', 'description': 'Before publication, a reviewer must confirm the producer/consumer contract and ensure that any migration retains decryption of required legacy records while new records carry the encryption-time IV.', 'kind': 'Configuration format and existing-record compatibility must be preserved.', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['CLM-004', 'CLM-005']}, {'category': 'compatibility_contract', 'description': 'A reviewer must establish which existing records and producers must remain decryptable before changing IV generation or record layout.', 'kind': 'Existing configuration records or external configuration producers may require the current fixed-IV convention.', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['CLM-004', 'CLM-005']}], 'digest_contract_assessment': {'security_relevance': 'false', 'contract_kind': 'unknown', 'expected_digest_source': '', 'backend_repository_available': False, 'backend_change_required': False, 'client_only_change_safe': False, 'rollout_strategy': '', 'pull_request_note': ''}, 'review_assumptions': ['The reviewed current-record format is version byte `1`, followed by one AES-CBC block (16 bytes for AES) of IV material and ciphertext; the corresponding producer must emit this layout.', 'Legacy configuration records are ciphertext-only AES-CBC records encrypted with the all-zero IV and therefore have a non-empty length divisible by the AES block size.', 'The length-disjoint framing is required to preserve complete legacy ciphertext compatibility: a current record has total length congruent to one modulo the AES block size, while a legacy ciphertext length is congruent to zero.', 'A malformed record that is structurally indistinguishable from a legacy ciphertext (for example, an arbitrary block-aligned byte sequence beginning with `1`) remains subject to the legacy path; without an authenticated producer-defined marker, it cannot be distinguished from existing legacy ciphertext without breaking legacy compatibility.', "The planned test source compiles in the module's Kotlin test friend context and can invoke the newly `internal` test seam.", 'Approval requires confirmation that decrypted configuration payloads remain encoded as two newline-separated strings; the supplied `General.parseConfig` API surface establishes the two-string callback but does not provide the plaintext serialization source.', 'Approval requires confirmation that version-1 records are produced as `[0x01][16-byte IV][AES/CBC/PKCS5Padding ciphertext]` and that legacy ciphertext-only records use the zero-IV compatibility path, as required by the provided production-file contract.', 'The malformed 16-byte record beginning with version 1 is expected to be rejected as an incomplete current envelope rather than reinterpreted as a legacy ciphertext, per the supplied malformed-current-record contract.'], 'review_blockers': [], 'required_tests': ['In `src/test/java/org/quantumbadger/redreader/test/general/GeneralConfigCiphertextFormatTest.kt`, verify two valid version-1 records with distinct carried 16-byte IVs each decrypt to their own key/value pair through `General.parseConfig`.', 'In `src/test/java/org/quantumbadger/redreader/test/general/GeneralConfigCiphertextFormatTest.kt`, verify a legacy block-aligned ciphertext encrypted with the all-zero IV still invokes the callback with its decoded key/value pair.', 'In `src/test/java/org/quantumbadger/redreader/test/general/GeneralConfigCiphertextFormatTest.kt`, verify empty records, unsupported version-1-shaped envelopes, incomplete version-1 envelopes, and invalid record lengths do not invoke the callback.', '`currentRecordsDecryptUsingTheirCarriedIvs` verifies separate version-1 records encrypted with distinct fresh IVs decode their corresponding callback values.', '`legacyZeroIvRecordsRemainSupported` verifies ciphertext-only, zero-IV legacy compatibility decoding.', '`malformedOrUnsupportedCurrentEnvelopesDoNotInvokeTheAction` verifies empty, unsupported-version, incomplete/missing-IV, and non-block-aligned records are rejected without callback invocation.'], 'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'manual_review_required': True, 'auto_apply': False, 'publication_allowed': False, 'publication_status': 'blocked', 'semantic_validation': {'status': 'valid', 'errors': [], 'warnings': []}, 'stored_value_contract': {}, 'fix_scope': 'validation_only', 'status': 'SUCCESS', 'error': None, 'original_method_body': '\tprivate fun parseConfig(b1: ByteArray, b2: ByteArray, action: (String, String) -> Unit) {\n\t\ttry {\n\t\t\tval cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/CBC/PKCS5PADDING")\n\t\t\tcipher.init(\n\t\t\t\tCipher.DECRYPT_MODE,\n\t\t\t\tSecretKeySpec(b1, "AES"),\n\t\t\t\tIvParameterSpec(ByteArray(16))\n\t\t\t)\n\t\t\tval dis = DataInputStream(ByteArrayInputStream(cipher.doFinal(b2)))\n\t\t\tval key = dis.readUTF()\n\t\t\tval value = dis.readUTF()\n\n\t\t\taction(key, value)\n\n\t\t} catch(_: Exception) {}\n\t}\n', 'corrected_method_body': '\t@JvmStatic\n\tinternal fun parseConfig(b1: ByteArray, b2: ByteArray, action: (String, String) -> Unit) {\n\t\ttry {\n\t\t\tval cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/CBC/PKCS5PADDING")\n\t\t\tval blockSize = cipher.blockSize\n\t\t\tval iv: ByteArray\n\t\t\tval ciphertext: ByteArray\n\n\t\t\twhen (b2.size % blockSize) {\n\t\t\t\t0 -> {\n\t\t\t\t\t// Legacy records contain only AES-CBC ciphertext and used an all-zero IV.\n\t\t\t\t\tif (b2.isEmpty()) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\tiv = ByteArray(blockSize)\n\t\t\t\t\tciphertext = b2\n\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t1 -> {\n\t\t\t\t\t// Current records are [version][IV][AES-CBC ciphertext].\n\t\t\t\t\tval version = b2[0].toInt() and 0xff\n\t\t\t\t\tif (version != 1) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t\tval ivEnd = 1 + blockSize\n\t\t\t\t\tif (b2.size <= ivEnd || (b2.size - ivEnd) % blockSize != 0) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t\tiv = b2.copyOfRange(1, ivEnd)\n\t\t\t\t\tciphertext = b2.copyOfRange(ivEnd, b2.size)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\telse -> return\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tcipher.init(\n\t\t\t\tCipher.DECRYPT_MODE,\n\t\t\t\tSecretKeySpec(b1, "AES"),\n\t\t\t\tIvParameterSpec(iv)\n\t\t\t)\n\t\t\tval dis = DataInputStream(ByteArrayInputStream(cipher.doFinal(ciphertext)))\n\t\t\tval key = dis.readUTF()\n\t\t\tval value = dis.readUTF()\n\n\t\t\taction(key, value)\n\n\t\t} catch(_: Exception) {}\n\t}\n', 'finding_id': '5f26ffaee5d9', 'branch': 'fix/parseconfig-ivparameterspecspec-5f26ffaee5d9-d161ae24db', 'base_branch': 'master', 'base_commit': '3a1ab4f32a763155c49fa233cd1314173abd22d9', 'solution_revision': 'd161ae24db', 'worktree_attempt': 1, 'orphaned_worktree_paths': [], 'worktree_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final/finding_worktrees/org.quantumbadger.redreader_117.apk/5f26ffaee5d9/d161ae24db', 'base_repository_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/exp_final/clones/org.quantumbadger.redreader_117.apk', 'coordinated_edits': [{'source_file': 'src/main/java/org/quantumbadger/redreader/common/General.kt', 'symbol': 'General.parseConfig', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '\tprivate fun parseConfig(b1: ByteArray, b2: ByteArray, action: (String, String) -> Unit) {\n\t\ttry {\n\t\t\tval cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/CBC/PKCS5PADDING")\n\t\t\tcipher.init(\n\t\t\t\tCipher.DECRYPT_MODE,\n\t\t\t\tSecretKeySpec(b1, "AES"),\n\t\t\t\tIvParameterSpec(ByteArray(16))\n\t\t\t)\n\t\t\tval dis = DataInputStream(ByteArrayInputStream(cipher.doFinal(b2)))\n\t\t\tval key = dis.readUTF()\n\t\t\tval value = dis.readUTF()\n\n\t\t\taction(key, value)\n\n\t\t} catch(_: Exception) {}\n\t}\n', 'corrected_code': '\t@JvmStatic\n\tinternal fun parseConfig(b1: ByteArray, b2: ByteArray, action: (String, String) -> Unit) {\n\t\ttry {\n\t\t\tval cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/CBC/PKCS5PADDING")\n\t\t\tval blockSize = cipher.blockSize\n\t\t\tval iv: ByteArray\n\t\t\tval ciphertext: ByteArray\n\n\t\t\twhen (b2.size % blockSize) {\n\t\t\t\t0 -> {\n\t\t\t\t\t// Legacy records contain only AES-CBC ciphertext and used an all-zero IV.\n\t\t\t\t\tif (b2.isEmpty()) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\tiv = ByteArray(blockSize)\n\t\t\t\t\tciphertext = b2\n\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t1 -> {\n\t\t\t\t\t// Current records are [version][IV][AES-CBC ciphertext].\n\t\t\t\t\tval version = b2[0].toInt() and 0xff\n\t\t\t\t\tif (version != 1) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t\tval ivEnd = 1 + blockSize\n\t\t\t\t\tif (b2.size <= ivEnd || (b2.size - ivEnd) % blockSize != 0) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t\tiv = b2.copyOfRange(1, ivEnd)\n\t\t\t\t\tciphertext = b2.copyOfRange(ivEnd, b2.size)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\telse -> return\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tcipher.init(\n\t\t\t\tCipher.DECRYPT_MODE,\n\t\t\t\tSecretKeySpec(b1, "AES"),\n\t\t\t\tIvParameterSpec(iv)\n\t\t\t)\n\t\t\tval dis = DataInputStream(ByteArrayInputStream(cipher.doFinal(ciphertext)))\n\t\t\tval key = dis.readUTF()\n\t\t\tval value = dis.readUTF()\n\n\t\t\taction(key, value)\n\n\t\t} catch(_: Exception) {}\n\t}\n', 'reason': 'Replaces the direct fixed-size IV passed to every decryption with validated decoding of the current versioned record envelope and its carried IV. It retains a separate, explicit zero-IV branch for block-aligned legacy ciphertext records and exposes the unchanged entry-point name as an internal Kotlin test seam.'}, {'source_file': 'src/test/java/org/quantumbadger/redreader/test/general/GeneralConfigCiphertextFormatTest.kt', 'symbol': 'GeneralConfigCiphertextFormatTest', 'edit_kind': 'create', 'original_code': '', 'corrected_code': 'package org.quantumbadger.redreader.common\n\nimport java.security.SecureRandom\nimport javax.crypto.Cipher\nimport javax.crypto.spec.IvParameterSpec\nimport javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec\nimport org.junit.Assert.assertEquals\nimport org.junit.Assert.assertFalse\nimport org.junit.Assert.assertTrue\nimport org.junit.Test\n\nclass GeneralConfigCiphertextFormatTest {\n\n    @Test\n    fun currentRecordsDecryptUsingTheirCarriedIvs() {\n        val firstIv = freshIv()\n        val secondIv = freshIv()\n        assertFalse(firstIv.contentEquals(secondIv))\n\n        val firstRecord = currentRecord(firstIv, "first-client\\nfirst-secret")\n        val secondRecord = currentRecord(secondIv, "second-client\\nsecond-secret")\n\n        assertEquals(\n            listOf("first-client" to "first-secret"),\n            parse(firstRecord)\n        )\n        assertEquals(\n            listOf("second-client" to "second-secret"),\n            parse(secondRecord)\n        )\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun legacyZeroIvRecordsRemainSupported() {\n        val legacyRecord = encrypt(ByteArray(AES_BLOCK_SIZE), "legacy-client\\nlegacy-secret")\n\n        assertEquals(\n            listOf("legacy-client" to "legacy-secret"),\n            parse(legacyRecord)\n        )\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun malformedOrUnsupportedCurrentEnvelopesDoNotInvokeTheAction() {\n        val iv = freshIv()\n        val ciphertext = encrypt(iv, "current-client\\ncurrent-secret")\n        val malformedRecords = listOf(\n            ByteArray(0),\n            byteArrayOf(2) + iv + ciphertext,\n            byteArrayOf(CURRENT_VERSION) + ByteArray(AES_BLOCK_SIZE - 1),\n            byteArrayOf(CURRENT_VERSION) + iv,\n            byteArrayOf(CURRENT_VERSION) + iv + byteArrayOf(0)\n        )\n\n        malformedRecords.forEachIndexed { index, record ->\n            assertTrue("malformed record $index invoked the action", parse(record).isEmpty())\n        }\n    }\n\n    private fun parse(record: ByteArray): List<Pair<String, String>> {\n        val values = mutableListOf<Pair<String, String>>()\n        General.parseConfig(KEY, record) { first, second ->\n            values += first to second\n        }\n        return values\n    }\n\n    private fun currentRecord(iv: ByteArray, plaintext: String): ByteArray {\n        return byteArrayOf(CURRENT_VERSION) + iv + encrypt(iv, plaintext)\n    }\n\n    private fun encrypt(iv: ByteArray, plaintext: String): ByteArray {\n        val cipher = Cipher.getInstance(CIPHER_TRANSFORMATION)\n        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, SecretKeySpec(KEY, "AES"), IvParameterSpec(iv))\n        return cipher.doFinal(plaintext.toByteArray(Charsets.UTF_8))\n    }\n\n    private fun freshIv(): ByteArray {\n        return ByteArray(AES_BLOCK_SIZE).also(SECURE_RANDOM::nextBytes)\n    }\n\n    private companion object {\n        private const val AES_BLOCK_SIZE = 16\n        private const val CURRENT_VERSION: Byte = 1\n        private const val CIPHER_TRANSFORMATION = "AES/CBC/PKCS5Padding"\n\n        private val SECURE_RANDOM = SecureRandom()\n        private val KEY = byteArrayOf(\n            0x00, 0x01, 0x02, 0x03,\n            0x04, 0x05, 0x06, 0x07,\n            0x08, 0x09, 0x0a, 0x0b,\n            0x0c, 0x0d, 0x0e, 0x0f\n        )\n    }\n}\n', 'reason': 'Adds JUnit coverage for version-1 IV-carrying configuration records with distinct fresh IVs, retained zero-IV legacy ciphertext records, and the required empty, unsupported-version, missing/incomplete-IV, and non-block-aligned envelope rejection cases. Declaring the test in `org.quantumbadger.redreader.common` provides direct package-module access to the coordinated internal `General.parseConfig` seam without an unavailable `General` import.'}], 'changed_files': ['src/main/java/org/quantumbadger/redreader/common/General.kt', 'src/test/java/org/quantumbadger/redreader/test/general/GeneralConfigCiphertextFormatTest.kt'], 'quality_score': 100, 'explanation': '<!-- pr-title: Read IVs from versioned configuration records -->\nI found that `parseConfig` decrypted every configuration record with a new all-zero 16-byte IV. The analysis rule requires an IV from a randomized source, so using the same fixed IV did not meet that rule.\n\nI changed `parseConfig` to read the IV from version-1 `[version][IV][ciphertext]` records and validate the envelope before decrypting. I retained an explicit zero-IV path for non-empty, block-aligned legacy ciphertext and reject empty, unsupported, incomplete, and malformed inputs. I also added tests for records carrying distinct IVs and for the legacy format.', 'applied_timestamp': '2026-10-22T17:36:06.822379+00:00'}, {'apk_name': 'org.quantumbadger.redreader_117.apk', 'method_name': 'parseConfig', 'csv_class': 'org.quantumbadger.redreader.common.General', 'source_file': 'src/main/java/org/quantumbadger/redreader/common/General.kt', 'spec': 'SecretKeySpecSpec', 'error_message': 'the keyMaterial given to SecretKeySpec(byte[], String) was not observed to have been prepared by a Key.getEncoded()', 'tool': 'ape', 'detector_context': {'code': 'SECRETKEYSPEC-NOBS-00', 'site_kind': 'NOBS: a required origin was not observed (not a positive contradiction)', 'label': 'not-observed', 'label_meaning': 'NOT OBSERVED: the runtime monitor tracks the producers a rule requires by object identity within one process, and saw none for this object. No admitted producer was seen (e.g. SecureRandom for an IV, salt or seed; Key.getEncoded() for key bytes). The monitor cannot tell innocent cases -- bytes read back from storage, an IV parsed from the ciphertext, a producer it does not see -- from the defective one: bytes that are constants compiled into the application or derived from constants. Where the bytes come from decides it.', 'expected': 'prepared key material', 'source_location': 'General.kt:701', 'runtime_observation': 'Reported in 99 run(s) of the app, every run of the campaign; each run starts from a clean, read-only emulator. Fingerprint of the byte[] material (vfp; the value itself is not logged): 1 distinct value(s) over 99 reporting run(s). One value across runs means constant material on this one emulated device; varying values mean bytes generated or read at run time. Mechanical constant check of this site (SECRETKEYSPEC-NOBS-00): verdict=constant; evidence: runs=99; distinct_vfp=1; vfp=sha256:b8b676364232f095'}, 'repository_guidance': [{'path': 'CONTRIBUTING.md', 'content': '# Contributing\n\nPull requests for RedReader are always gratefully received. New pull requests\nare reviewed whenever @QuantumBadger gets some spare time, which is usually\nwithin a couple of weeks of submitting (apologies if it takes longer!)\n\n## Getting a Reddit API key\n\nAn API key is required to connect to Reddit. It\'s possible to acquire this from the\nfollowing link:\n\nhttps://old.reddit.com/prefs/apps\n\nCreate an app with the type "Installed app" at the above page, and note the ID.\nAlso set the Redirect URI to "redreader://rr_oauth_redir".\n\nYou can set the ID at build time, or at runtime.\n\n### At build time\n\n* Copy the file [src/main/assets/reddit_auth.placeholder.txt] to [src/main/assets/reddit_auth.txt]\n* Put your ID inside [src/main/assets/reddit_auth.txt]\n\nBe careful not to commit this file to git, as this could expose your key.\n\n### At runtime\n\nGo to `Settings > Network > Reddit client ID override` and enter your ID there.\n\n## What is accepted?\n\nPlease submit pull requests for:\n\n* :heavy_check_mark: **New features**\n* :heavy_check_mark: **Bug fixes**\n* :heavy_check_mark: **Significant performance improvements**\n* :heavy_check_mark: **New unit tests**\n\nPull requests for the following things may be rejected:\n\n* ❌ **Translations into other languages** -- please submit these using\n    [Weblate](https://hosted.weblate.org/engage/redreader) to avoid conflicts!\n    \n* ❌ **Rewording existing English strings** -- whether the new wording is better\n    or not is normally subjective. This includes README/other metadata changes.\n    If you notice a typo or other mistake, please raise an issue on GitHub.\n    \n* ❌ **Code formatting changes** -- e.g. changing tabs to spaces, making\n    trivial changes to the structure of code, or refactoring that isn\'t part of\n    one of the accepted changes above.\n    \n* ❌ **Micro-optimisations** -- changes that don\'t have obviously significant\n    performance benefits should be accompanied by benchmark results!\n\n## Check before submitting\n\nRedReader uses a number of automated code checks. You can run these locally\nusing the `pmd`, `checkstyle`, `lint`, and `test` Gradle targets:\n\n```\n./gradlew pmd checkstyle lint test\n```\n\nThese checks are run automatically on every pull request, so please ensure they\npass before submitting!\n\n## Style guidelines\n\nFor Java files, please:\n\n* Use tabs for indentation\n* Limit line length to 100 characters\n* Try to match the style of existing code\n\nFor XML files, there are no restrictions on tabs vs spaces or line length, but\nplease try to stay consistent with the file you\'re editing.\n\nFor new Java or XML files:\n\n* Add a GPLv3 copyright message to the top of the file (you can copy this from\n    an existing Java or XML file)'}], 'branch_policy': {}, 'compatibility_policy': {}, 'migration_assessment': {'usage_kind': 'unknown', 'evidence': ['`parseConfig` constructs a `javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec` from `b1` and the literal algorithm string `"AES"`.', "The governed construction matches the specification's c1 two-argument event shape, and `AES` is an allowed specification algorithm value.", 'The `b1` argument is sourced from an `appIds(context)` digest output at the supplied direct caller.', 'The runtime measurement observed a single byte-material fingerprint at the governed call across 99 reporting runs on the measured emulator campaign.', 'The supplied specification does not define what source facts establish `preparedKeyMaterial` or `randomized`, nor does it define how `offset` and `len` are evaluated for c1.', 'The source uses the constructed key and a newly allocated `ByteArray(16)` IV to initialize an AES/CBC/PKCS5PADDING cipher in decrypt mode.'], 'legacy_compatibility_required': True, 'safe_strategy': "Do not change the key bytes, derivation, or cipher input until the detector's required-provenance semantics are established and the encrypted-configuration compatibility contract is known. A randomized replacement is not forward compatible unless it preserves decryption of the configuration bytes processed by this method.", 'policy_authorized': False}, 'publication_considerations': [{'category': 'compatibility_contract', 'description': 'The reviewed method decrypts configuration input with this key, but the packet does not establish the producer, persisted-data lifetime, or external consumer contract. Build and source recheck cannot validate those contracts.', 'kind': 'A change to b1 or its derivation must preserve decryption of the configuration bytes supplied as b2, including any persisted or externally produced configuration records.', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['CLM-003', 'CLM-007']}], 'digest_contract_assessment': {'security_relevance': 'false', 'contract_kind': 'unknown', 'expected_digest_source': '', 'backend_repository_available': False, 'backend_change_required': False, 'client_only_change_safe': False, 'rollout_strategy': '', 'pull_request_note': ''}, 'review_assumptions': ['SecretKeySpec defensively copies its cons